  "label": "Harmful",
  "description": "The meme may unintentionally reinforce 'inspiration porn' tropes — portraying the disabled person as needing to be 'inspirational' or 'different' to be accepted, rather than simply being a person with a disability who is equal in worth and capability. The juxtaposition of the text with the image of a person in a wheelchair can be seen as a form of ableism, as it may imply that the person's disability is somehow 'not normal' or 'not different' — which is a problematic framing. The meme may also unintentionally normalize the idea that disability is something to be 'overcome' or 'fixed,' rather than accepted as part of a person's identity.",
